---
description: UI text ≥72% and icons ≥56% opacity for accessibility contrast
alwaysApply: true
---

# Opacity floors: text 72%, icons 56%

Never style **text** below **72% opacity** (alpha ≥ `0.72`), or **icons** below **56% opacity** (alpha ≥ `0.56`). These floors are an internal accessibility policy: lower alpha can reduce contrast and legibility depending on foreground/background compositing, and often reads as disabled.

## Text (≥ 0.72)

- `color` set with `rgba()` / `hsla()` alpha below `0.72`
- `opacity` on elements whose primary content is text (labels, helpers, captions, placeholders styled as copy)
- Figma text color variables with an opacity suffix below 72 — clamp to **0.72** or higher instead of matching the file literally

```scss
// ❌ BAD — secondary text too faint
color: rgba(var(--center-channel-color-rgb), 0.64);
opacity: 0.5; // on a text label

// ✅ GOOD — muted but still ≥ 72%
color: rgba(var(--center-channel-color-rgb), 0.72);
color: var(--center-channel-color); // full opacity when hierarchy allows
```

## Icons (≥ 0.56)

- Icon `color` / `fill` with alpha below `0.56`
- `opacity` on icon elements or icon wrappers
- Figma icon color variables with an opacity suffix below 56 — clamp to **0.56** or higher

```scss
// ❌ BAD
color: rgba(var(--center-channel-color-rgb), 0.48);
opacity: 0.4; // on an icon

// ✅ GOOD
color: rgba(var(--center-channel-color-rgb), 0.56);
color: rgba(var(--center-channel-color-rgb), 0.72);
```

## Does not apply to

Non-text, non-icon surfaces may use lower alpha: backgrounds, borders, fills, overlays, and decorative strokes.

## Motion exception

Entrance/exit keyframes may temporarily fade text or icons below these floors. Resting, visible UI must land at **≥ 0.72** for text and **≥ 0.56** for icons.
